{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533798-magic-locking","id":1533798,"title":"Magic locking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-08T00:39:43-07:00","id":1533798,"title":"Magic locking","content":"Hello! A few questions i can seem to sort out. Non RAW answers are welcome. :<br /> <br /> 1 . Does pattern locking allow automatic hits for spells like curses, combustion etc?<br /> <br /> 2. At what sphere levels does pattern locking work for each pattern?<br /> <br /> 3. How many successes does it cost to lock a pattern?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T11:19:15-07:00","id":1533829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533798-magic-locking#post1533798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! A few questions i can seem to sort out. Non RAW answers are welcome. :<br /> <br /> 1 . Does pattern locking allow automatic hits for spells like curses, combustion etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but most spells you would lock like that don\u2019t need aiming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. At what sphere levels does pattern locking work for each pattern? </div> </div> </div>M20 dropped the ball on this and never gave an answer. That said, just about every example in the core book that can be viewed as locking uses rank 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. How many successes does it cost to lock a pattern? </div> </div> </div>None given. At most 1 success I think, but I don\u2019t even charge for it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 04-09-2024, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T13:43:50-07:00","id":1533850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533798-magic-locking?p=1533829#post1533829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but most spells you would lock like that don\u2019t need aiming.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How does the not aiming work?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T06:41:14-07:00","id":1533885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533798-magic-locking?p=1533850#post1533850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the not aiming work?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, aiming with magick in general implies conjuring a sort of external physical attack that can reasonably miss or be dodged.<br /> <br /> Like, say, magical bullet or a fireball can miss when fired towards a target, especially if the target it's active and good at not to getting hit. This would typically be represented by an attack roll, which can fail or be contested by a Dodge (say, using Firearms + Dex to shoot the magick bullet).<br /> <br /> Magickal attacks that don't use Skills to hit allow the target to use Dodge to cancel the Arete roll directly (but cancelling all successes doesn't mean that the spell fails to be casted, just that it fails to hit the target).<br /> <br /> That's aiming rules. So curses, combustion...can they miss or be dodged?.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it depends on ST judgement, but I would argue most of times you don't need to &quot;aim&quot; a curse ... unless the mage needs to point\u200b with the finger, wand, or something, maybe.<br /> <br /> Just like how you don't need to roll to &quot;aim&quot; a personal insult (and the target tipically doesn't get to &quot;Dodge&quot; it), if someone wants to hurt you by directing &quot;ill feelings&quot; towards you, by pinching a voodo doll, attacking your name ... etc. That's not something you can &quot;move away&quot; from&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T08:40:38-07:00","id":1533888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533798-magic-locking?p=1533885#post1533885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's aiming rules. So curses, combustion...can they miss or be dodged?.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it depends on ST judgement, but I would argue most of times you don't need to &quot;aim&quot; a curse ... unless the mage needs to point with the finger, wand, or something, maybe.<br /> <br /> Just like how you don't need to roll to &quot;aim&quot; a personal insult (and the target tipically doesn't get to &quot;Dodge&quot; it), if someone wants to hurt you by directing &quot;ill feelings&quot; towards you, by pinching a voodo doll, attacking your name ... etc. That's not something you can &quot;move away&quot; from&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So a self-combustion is always better than throwing a fireball cause you dont lose your successes and you cant miss?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T09:16:42-07:00","id":1533890,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on what you're aiming for :P.<br /> <br /> *A fireball could land on an area, and that could be circumnstantially better.<br /> <br /> *Shooting fire from a weapon that looks like it could shoot fire would require a roll, but it's also very likely to be Coincidental. Instant combustion could be, but I think it would be a harder sell, even if an ST lets it pass on the grounds it actually happens IRL altrough super rarely, it could incur instantly on Domino Effect (increasing the diff of additional cast).<br /> <br /> *If the magick comes from an attack (a punch, a gunshot) and the magick it's about causing damage, the damage of the magick replaces the damage from the attack (it's usually higger anyway), BUT if the magick does some other thing then the attack causes damage as normall, and the spell lands as normal (which could be circumnstantially better)<br /> <br /> Arguably, with Kung Fu magick or something like that, you could cast a spell <i>while dodging/parrying. </i><br /> <br /> In either case<i>, </i>while both the Arete and the roll will need to be successfull, the roll may have it's own benefits.<br /> <br /> One gripe I have from that rule it's the idea of Dodge taking aways sucesses from Arete. That's unablanced because Arete tends to be too small, and also because Arete it's determining other factors, like damage or duration, and it's not very clear to me what happens with those.The magick roll it's not really a good sustitute for an attack roll - I would houserule that away, and instead find an appropiate Ability + Attribute to roll for things that could be dodged","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-09-2024, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T13:01:20-07:00","id":1533897,"title":"","content":"And note that most of these spells we are discussing are nigh instantaneous. There's no need and no benefit to locking a spell like that as it doesn't need to travel with the subject nor does it stick around long enough to be a drain on the mage's concentration. Locking becomes important when spells have duration.<br /> <br /> There are offensive spells that could reasonably be locked to a subject, like a slow moving fireball that always moves towards someone, but these are considerably rarer than the instantaneous kind,<br /> <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> On another note, M20 says you only need locking when the spell doesn't already include the sphere that governs the pattern you are locking to. This is, in my opinion, a poor way of understanding what is going on. You can look at it that way, but I find a better way of saying this is that the locking rules are still being used. That is, a Life 4 spell to make someone bald is actually a Life 4/Life 2 spell but we only state the highest rank of the sphere needed.<br /> <br /> Ultimately both explanations work, so use whichever one is easier to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T14:29:44-07:00","id":1533904,"title":"","content":"Intersting. I wanted to use locking for 2 things:<ul><li>Locking a spell for it to persist on a moving target - examples - curses, buffs</li> </ul><ul><li>Locking a spell to auto hit (without aming) - examples - combustion, turning someone into a lightning rod (electromagnetic wise) so all lightning attacks autohit</li> </ul>Then again i have another question about Matter this time: If i melt a wall with Matter turning it to liquid, Will the magic turn back into a wall in the exact same shape when the effect is off?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-09-2024, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T14:44:00-07:00","id":1533905,"title":"","content":"Exact same shape as the wall used to be? Or exact same shape as the liquid is now?<br /> <br /> It should be that second one. The general idea is that when a spell ends, the effects of the spell end but anything that happened because of those effects persists. A thrown fireball lights things on fire and that fire persists after the fireball spell ends. A magical jetpack might cease working but the person wearing it doesn't go back to their launch point, they just fall. Turn a wall into liquid and it only stays liquid for the duration of the spell, but the shape it takes because it is a liquid persists.<br /> <br /> But there's a lot of wiggle room in this so do what most fits the paradigm of the spell and the needs of your table.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T15:27:39-07:00","id":1533907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1533798-magic-locking?p=1533905#post1533905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exact same shape as the wall used to be? Or exact same shape as the liquid is now?<br /> <br /> It should be that second one. The general idea is that when a spell ends, the effects of the spell end but anything that happened because of those effects persists. A thrown fireball lights things on fire and that fire persists after the fireball spell ends. A magical jetpack might cease working but the person wearing it doesn't go back to their launch point, they just fall. Turn a wall into liquid and it only stays liquid for the duration of the spell, but the shape it takes because it is a liquid persists.<br /> <br /> But there's a lot of wiggle room in this so do what most fits the paradigm of the spell and the needs of your table.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If so then what would hapen after the magic runs of on a spell that changes cardboard to metal or metal mace into a metal chain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-10-2024, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:28:02-07:00","id":1533971,"title":"","content":"We are delving into one of the fuzzy areas of the Mage rules. There are some changes that seem like they should be permanent. If a mage turns a brick into a rock, intuitively it seems it should stay a rock and there's often no dramatic consequence to it staying a rock. On the other hand, in folklore there are examples of permanent transformations and temporary ones. Alchemists sought to turn lead into gold permanently, but faerie gold only lasted a short time.<br /> <br /> The short answer is that the duration rules exist and are the default. Spells run out and we have to figure out what that means. The main options I see are:<br /> <br /> 1) Reality returns to what it was<br /> <br /> When the spell wears out reality gets as close as possible to what it was. The liquified wall would return to close to its original shape, the metal would go back to cardboard, and the chain returns to a mace. This doesn't generally match examples from the book, but it is an option.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) The direct effects stop, any consequences remain<br /> <br /> This is the description I gave before. When the spell runs out, it's direct effects end. This gets a little tricky based on what we count as the direct effects. The direct effect of the wall melt was turning it liquid, so it goes back to solid. The direct effect of the cardboard to metal was changing the material, so it goes back to cardboard.<br /> <br /> Changing a mace to a chain could be several things. It could be directly changing the form, in which case it will revert, or it could be making it malleable and quickly using that malleability to change its shape, in which case the shape stays. Use whichever one is mechanically and paradigmatically appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3) Reality returns to the closest normal<br /> <br /> In this scenario reality takes the simplest path to normality. The metal chain stays a chain because that is normal. The melted wall becomes a solid wall or a solid pile of bricks, whatever is closest to its melted shape because neither a liquid wall or a melted looking wall is normal.<br /> <br /> <br /> 4) Do it by feel<br /> <br /> Some things feel like they should be permanent without issue and some do not. Go with your gut on which is which. My gut says the melting wall is too strange and will eventually go back to solid, while there's nothing abnormal about solid metal so the cardboard to metal and metal chain can stay.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regardless of which method you choose, you are going to get into situations where you have to make a judgement call. I say, go with 2, 3, or 4 and make adjustments as necessary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:44:46-07:00","id":1533973,"title":"","content":"This was a lot of help. Thank you!<br /> I think ill go with 4.<br /> As for durations we dont really use them in our games. Instead we use sort of concentration rule: A mage ma have up to his Wits in active effects. Each effect increases the casting difficulty by +1. Pattern locking does not negate this and is used for locking moving targets. Only triggering with Time 4 is excused from the effect cap. The mage may release any and all effects at any time durring his turn.<br /> So we dont really use the Succeses= duration rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}